    LINEAGE: util/grub-mkrescue: Also use the x86 platforms next to the --directory one
    
    When the platform directory given with --directory is the x86 one of a
    tree that has one prefix per platform
    (<root>/<platform>/lib/grub/<platform>), also add the other x86
    platforms from <root> that exist. The image then boots on 32-bit UEFI
    firmware and on BIOS as well.
    
    This does not depend on the current directory, and does not replace
    platforms that were chosen explicitly.
    
